<title>BELGIUM: EU clears German/Dutch coal deal.</title>
<headline>EU clears German/Dutch coal deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had cleared a takeover deal involving firms in the German and Dutch coal industries.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Dutch SHV and Germany's Rheinbraun Brennstoff GmbH (RBB) take joint control of German firms Rheinbraun Thyssen Energy GmbH and Rheinbraun Thyssen Energy GmbH &amp; Co KG (RTE) and the Dutch firm SSM Coal B.V..</p>
<p>RBB, a coal trading company, is a subsidiary of Rhenbraun AG which is in turn a unit of RWE AG. SHV is also a coal trading company while the two RTE firms distribute coal products.</p>
<p>&quot;The investigation carried out has shown that the operation will not give any power to the parties to increase prices or to evade the rules of competition...,&quot; the Commission said. &quot;The proposed operation will not give power to the parties to impede competition in the EU.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
